{
    "name": "pc-status",
    "title": "PC status",
    "description": "PC status: a page on the rail with this computer's CPU, memory, GPU, and how steady its internet link is (macOS). While a tab has the page open, the server samples every 2 seconds with fixed commands: vm_stat, sysctl, ioreg, ping -c 1 to 1.1.1.1 (one ICMP packet, no data of yours), and optionally sudo -n /usr/bin/powermetrics, which runs only if you added a passwordless sudoers line for exactly that command. It reads no files, has no other network use, and stores nothing.",
